    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45242.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "And I was actually in the legislature at the time when I was accepted. It was a two-year program. And I didn't want to give up my seat in the House of Representatives to go to school. And the Kennedy School actually allowed me to extend it out an extra year because I was a sitting legislator. So I was able to do it in a three-year program because I didn't live up there. I commuted back and forth for the three years. It was quite a challenge to balancing both my legislative duties and going to school and I'd go to school, drive up to school in the mornings for classes in the mornings and afternoons and drive back for legislative sessions.",
