    "turn_text": "Well, we've been able to add to the Pell grants. And so they've increased the amount that's available for Pell grants. The problem is college tuition has risen dramatically. And so the Pell grant doesn't go as far as it used to be that a Pell grant would cover the cost of tuition, say, for a four-year college or university. And that's not the case anymore. So we need to do more to make college more affordable. I'm glad to do about the Rhode Island Promise program that will pay for the first two years or so I'm going to the Green and College of Rhode Island. And I hope we can do more for the years three and four of a college degree, say, Rhode Island College or URI, and see eventually more assistance for that, if not completely paid for, at least significantly reducing the cost for students, because we can't price people out of the mark. No one should be denied the opportunity to go to college, receive, earn a college degree, and a better path forward just because they can't afford it. We have to make it affordable. Education is a great equalizer,",
