    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45242.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 78,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, so we've been through a lot. The country's been through a lot over the last few years and I'm very proud of the leadership of the Democrats and especially Joe Biden, what he's done and work to make sure that they were resources available to help people get through the pandemic. But also the infrastructure bill that was recently passed, biggest infrastructure bill in the history of the country, over half a trillion dollars that went into repairing our roads and bridges and schools and water infrastructure. And then recently we just passed the Inflation Reduction Act that is going to help to bring down inflation. It's going to help us to transition to a green energy economy. So there's things in them, both the short term and the long term. But if these are the things that we've people focus on, we'll realize how Democrats have been able to deliver for the people of this country and all the things that work that's done to help working families. I'm very proud of the role of the delegation that I've been able to play to help.",
